From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 04:01:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] downloads: reuse a download held by another entry with
 the same url

Sources such as XvXun expose each favourites folder as its own entry, so
the same video can appear under several entries. Downloads were keyed on
(entry title, episode name) only, so a video downloaded in one folder
showed as "not downloaded" everywhere else and would be fetched again.

- episodes.sq / ChapterRepository: getChaptersByUrls (batched IN query,
  500 urls per statement to stay under SQLite's variable limit).
- DownloadManager.findSharedDownloads: for not-downloaded episodes, find
  a finished download of the same url under another entry of the same
  source; buildVideoOrShared plays that file.
- Entry screen marks such episodes as downloaded (skipped for local and
  merged entries); the player and download-ahead use the same lookup.
- New switch "Reuse downloads across entries" (default on) in
  Settings > Downloads.

Deleting the episode from the entry that does not own the file is a
no-op; delete it from the entry that downloaded it.
